# Feature: onboarding (library root only)

On first launch, block the library until the user sets **`libraryRoot`** (absolute directory) and **`ingestMode`** (move or copy).

Do **not** ask for allowed folder names or a custom tag vocabulary. Folders and tags are YAMNet/AudioSet class names produced at ingest.

## Persistence

Save merged config (defaults + `libraryRoot`) to `{libraryRoot}/.Fieldy.json`. Validate against `config/config.schema.json`. `ConfigStore` still **loads** a leftover `{libraryRoot}/.soundly-lite.json` and `~/.soundly-lite/pointer.json` if the Fieldy files are missing. New saves always write Fieldy paths.

On `save_config`, create:

```
{libraryRoot}/Mixed/
```

Do not pre-create 521 class folders. Class folders appear when the first file is classified into that class.

## Config fields

- Required: `libraryRoot`
- Optional defaults: `confidenceThreshold` 0.3, `analyzeChunkSeconds` 60 (16 kHz chunk size for RAM stitching, **not** a skip-YAMNet gate), `ingestMode` `move` (`copy` leaves the dropped file in place and tags only the library copy), `dropzoneOnLaunch` true. `conflictDelta` may still appear in saved JSON but is unused.

No `folders[]`, no `allowedTags[]`, no `yamnetToFolderMap`, no `longFileSeconds` bypass.

## UI

`#onboarding` visible when `get_config.needsOnboarding`. Copy links **AudioSet class** to `https://research.google.com/audioset/dataset/index.html` (system browser). Examples: Siren, Animal, Speech. Do not mention Mixed on this screen. “The app never creates all AudioSet folders up front.” Native **Browse…** plus **When dropping files** (`ingestMode` move/copy) plus Save. `#library` hidden until save succeeds. After onboarding, **Settings** (`#dialog-settings`) can change library root, threshold, ingestMode, and dropzoneOnLaunch.

To force onboarding again: quit the app, delete `~/.Fieldy/pointer.json`. The old library folder can stay; delete it only if you want a clean disk. Restart Electron so Python reloads config from disk.
